#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Nagashino: Shitaragahara, 28 June 1575.  A sample game for the
Grognard engine.

Takeda Katsuyori has besieged the castle of Nagashino, and Oda
Nobunaga and Tokugawa Ieyasu have come to relieve it with three times
his numbers.  They don't come on: they build a palisade along the far
bank of the little Rengo stream and put thousands of matchlock men
behind it.  The Takeda horse, the most famous in Japan, must charge it.
Play either side against the computer, or against a friend at the same
screen.

Run it with ./nagashino (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.nagashino.json.  ./nagashino --selftest checks the map and
plays a game between two computer players.
"""

